TI  - Comprehensive evaluation of low-temperature tolerance of 50 quinoa germplasm materials at the germination stage
AU  - Jiang, R.
AU  - Liu, W.
AU  - Wang, W.
AU  - Du, X.
AU  - Yang, F.
AU  - Huang, J.
AU  - Wei, Y.
T2  - Pratacultural Science
AB  - To identify low-temperature tolerance indicators at the germination stage of quinoa (Chenopodium quinoa), establish a comprehensive evaluation system, and explore low-temperature tolerant germplasm resources, this study evaluated 50 quinoa germplasm materials by measuring seed germination rate, germination energy, germination index, and germination speed index under low-temperature stress. A comprehensive assessment was conducted using principal component analysis, membership function analysis, and cluster analysis. The results showed that under low-temperature stress, germination rate, germination energy, germination index, and germination speed index all decreased, with reductions of 64.35%, 27.20%, 100.62, and 2.01, respectively, compared withthe normal temperature control. The coefficient of variation for germination index and germination speed index both decreased by 15.23% under stress, indicating their potential as key indicators for evaluating low-temperature tolerance during quinoa germination. Based on membership function comprehensive evaluation, the 50 quinoa accessions were classified into four grades. Cluster analysis was used to further divide them into four categories, identifying nine accessions with strong low-temperature tolerance, 21 with moderate tolerance, 19 with weak tolerance, and one cold-sensitive accession. © (2026), (Editorial Office of Pratacultural Science). All rights reserved.
