AB  - Genetic diversity analysis of seven amaranth (Amaranthus cruentus L.) genotypes (Ames 1959 RRC 1, PI 566896 Komo, PI 511719 Niqua alegria chang, PI 511876 Huatle, PI 527567 IZ 32, PI 604558 Mapes 821, PI 612169 Tibet Yellow) was performed using random amplified polymorphic DNA (RAPD) method with twelve random primers under optimized conditions. A total of 86 fragments was generated by the twelve primers, with an average of 5.5 fragments per primer. Out of 86 amplified fragments, 66 fragments showed polymorphism among seven genotypes of amaranth (Amaranthus cruentus L.), which represents 76.7% polymorphism). The genetic similarities ranged from 52.0% (PI 511876 Huatle and PI 604558 Mapes 821) to 93.5% (Ames 1959 RRC 1 and PI 527567 IZ 32). According to the genetic distance data and UPGMA dendrogram, PI 511876 Huatle is the most diverse genotype and distinguishable with all primers used in the study.
